From febace670cd6cd746e6e8afda95c75ae2050d548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:59:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat(operator): CLI verbs on a Kernel-owned Safe through
 agent-signer

ADAPTATION item 7: one-shot verbs that build their own Safe broadcaster and
wallet -- `jinn tasks submit` (execution-context) and `jinn solver-plugins
publish|revoke|block|feedback` (PluginRegistryPublisher,
ReputationRegistryClient) -- use the hardware-signed Kernel account when
config.signer is set.

- signer: openCliKernelSafeBroadcaster -- KernelSafeBroadcaster on the
  daemon's own venue state (<earningDir>/../venue/venue.db): its broadcast
  lock is cross-process, so a verb and a daemon serialize on the Kernel, and
  the ledger reconciles what either left with an unknown outcome; refuses
  when the Kernel does not own the Safe.
- solver-plugins factories take `signer`; with it no keystore is decrypted
  (the reputation factory no longer needs a password for writes) and direct
  writes use createAgentSignerWalletClient.
- tests: the CLI broadcaster (ownership refusal, ledger in the daemon venue
  state); the Kernel-owner hermetic loop now runs the production
  solver-plugins publisher with a signer: after the Kernel (the agent NFT's
  owner) approves its Safe (setApprovalForAll), the ERC-8004 plugin record
  is written Safe-routed via agent-signer and read back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
